---
/**
 * Tooltip Component
 *
 * STATUS: KEPT AS REACT (src/components/ui/tooltip.tsx)
 *
 * RATIONALE FOR KEEPING AS REACT:
 * This component uses @radix-ui/react-tooltip which provides:
 * - Portal rendering for proper z-index layering
 * - Complex positioning logic (top, bottom, left, right with sideOffset)
 * - Hover/focus state management with delay timers
 * - Arrow/pointer indicators with proper positioning
 * - ARIA attributes and full accessibility support (role="tooltip")
 * - Composable sub-components (Provider, Trigger, Content)
 * - Animated open/close transitions
 * - Keyboard navigation support (Escape to close)
 * - Collision detection to keep tooltip visible in viewport
 *
 * Conversion Complexity Analysis:
 * - Estimated ~400-600 lines of vanilla JS/Alpine.js to replicate
 * - Extensive accessibility testing required
 * - Custom portal positioning implementation needed
 * - Hover delay logic and collision detection to implement from scratch
 * - Currently used in sidebar.tsx for collapsed sidebar tooltips
 *
 * Decision: Keep as React component with @astrojs/react integration
 * Use with `client:load` directive when needed in Astro pages
 *
 * USAGE IN ASTRO PAGES:
 * ```astro
 * ---
 * import { Tooltip, TooltipProvider, TooltipTrigger, TooltipContent } from '@/components/ui/tooltip';
 * ---
 *
 * <Tooltip client:load>
 *   <TooltipTrigger>Hover me</TooltipTrigger>
 *   <TooltipContent>
 *     <p>This is a tooltip</p>
 *   </TooltipContent>
 * </Tooltip>
 * ```
 *
 * PROPS:
 * - delayDuration?: number - Delay before showing tooltip (default: 0)
 * - side?: 'top' | 'right' | 'bottom' | 'left' - Position relative to trigger
 * - sideOffset?: number - Distance from trigger in px (default: 0)
 * - align?: 'start' | 'center' | 'end' - Alignment along the side
 * - alignOffset?: number - Offset from alignment position
 * - arrowPadding?: number - Padding between arrow and trigger edges
 * - avoidCollisions?: boolean - Enable collision detection
 *
 * ALTERNATIVES:
 * 1. Native HTML title attribute (simple, no positioning control):
 *    ```astro
 *    <button title="Simple tooltip">Button</button>
 *    ```
 *
 * 2. CSS-only tooltips (limited, no portal):
 *    ```astro
 *    <button data-tooltip="Tooltip text" class="has-tooltip">Button</button>
 *    ```
 *
 * 3. Tippy.js (lightweight alternative to Radix):
 *    ```bash
 *    npx astro add tippy.js
 *    ```
 */
